###
Media values for multimodal prompts: images, audio, video and documents.

A media value substituted into a model prompt (>>, <<, a typed capture or a > if: claim) is
attached before the prompt text, and the text shows only its name: the binding name, or
image_1, audio_1, ... for an unnamed value. Paths start at the working directory and follow
KEDI_WORKSPACE_POLICY like the filesystem module; .env files are refused.
###

```
from typing import Any

from kedi.media import Audio, Document, Image, Media, Video
```

@image(source: Any) -> Image:
    ###
    Load an image from a workspace path, an http(s) URL or a data: URI.

    Args:
        source (Any): A path relative to the working directory, a URL, a data URI or an image.

    Returns:
        Image: A PNG, JPEG, GIF or WebP image. Prompts attach it and show its name.
    ###
    = `Image.coerce(source)`

@audio(source: Any) -> Audio:
    ###
    Load audio from a workspace path, an http(s) URL or a data: URI.

    Args:
        source (Any): A path relative to the working directory, a URL, a data URI or audio.

    Returns:
        Audio: WAV, MP3, OGG, FLAC, AIFF or AAC audio. Gemini reads all of them; OpenAI audio
            models read WAV and MP3; Anthropic and Bedrock take no audio.
    ###
    = `Audio.coerce(source)`

@video(source: Any) -> Video:
    ###
    Load a video from a workspace path, an http(s) URL, a YouTube URL or a data: URI.

    Args:
        source (Any): A path relative to the working directory, a URL, a data URI or a video.

    Returns:
        Video: A video for Gemini or Bedrock Nova models. YouTube URLs go to Gemini as URLs.
    ###
    = `Video.coerce(source)`

@document(source: Any) -> Document:
    ###
    Load a PDF or a UTF-8 text document from a workspace path, an http(s) URL or a data: URI.

    Args:
        source (Any): A path relative to the working directory, a URL, a data URI or a document.

    Returns:
        Document: A PDF, read by the provider, or a text document (text, Markdown, CSV, HTML,
            JSON, XML, YAML, TOML), which reaches the model as delimited text.
    ###
    = `Document.coerce(source)`

